The tree of a page's named anchors (HTBTree) balanced as an AVL tree. Its balancing gave up after seven corrections
per insertion, and the anchors of a page, added in the page's order (cite_note-1, cite_ref-1, ...), made a tree
deep enough to take ~66 string comparisons to find or add one, where a balanced one takes ~22: on Wikipedia's
article on the 80386 (2,400 anchors) 155 -> 145 M instructions for lynx -dump. The order of the elements (equal ones
after those already there: directory listings) is unchanged.

